  data: {
    LLM: 'The player associated with the seven of diamonds starts, then play continues clockwise. On a turn, play one legal adjacent rank in a suit row or pass. Legal plays extend each suit outward from 7 toward K and A. Each player may pass at most three times; a player who must pass again while still holding cards goes bankrupt and is ranked behind active finishers.',
    Player: 'The player associated with the seven of diamonds starts, then play continues clockwise. On a turn, play one legal adjacent rank in a suit row or pass. Legal plays extend each suit outward from 7 toward K and A. Each player may pass at most three times; a player who must pass again while still holding cards goes bankrupt and is ranked behind active finishers.',
    objective: 'Empty your hand as early as possible while avoiding bankruptcy from overusing passes.',
    gameplay: 'The player associated with the seven of diamonds starts, then play continues clockwise. On a turn, play one legal adjacent rank in a suit row or pass. Legal plays extend each suit outward from 7 toward K and A. Each player may pass at most three times; a player who must pass again while still holding cards goes bankrupt and is ranked behind active finishers.',
    keyRules: [
      'All sevens are laid out before normal turns begin.',
      'Each player has a strict pass limit (typically three).',
      'Finishing order determines ranking; bankrupt players are last.',
